 "subs": [
  {
   "id": "l01_0",
   "line": "l01",
   "text": "In 1637, a single Dutch flower bulb could sell for as much as a house.",
   "t0": 0.35,
   "t1": 5.99
  },
  {
   "id": "l02_1",
   "line": "l02",
   "text": "Not gold. Not diamonds. A tulip.",
   "t0": 6.55,
   "t1": 9.69
  },
  {
   "id": "l03_2",
   "line": "l03",
   "text": "Tulips had come from the Ottoman Empire, and the Dutch fell in love with them.",
   "t0": 10.15,
   "t1": 15.33
  },
  {
   "id": "l04_3",
   "line": "l04",
   "text": "The rarest ones had flames of colour across their petals.",
   "t0": 15.85,
   "t1": 19.71
  },
  {
   "id": "l04_4",
   "line": "l04",
   "text": "And no one could predict which bulb would bloom like that.",
   "t0": 19.75,
   "t1": 23.53
  },
  {
   "id": "l05_5",
   "line": "l05",
   "text": "So people began to bet.",
   "t0": 23.95,
   "t1": 25.89
  },
  {
   "id": "l06_6",
   "line": "l06",
   "text": "They traded in taverns, through the winter, while the bulbs were still in the ground.",
   "t0": 26.45,
   "t1": 31.53
  },
  {
   "id": "l06_7",
   "line": "l06",
   "text": "Buying flowers nobody had seen.",
   "t0": 31.71,
   "t1": 34.13
  },
  {
   "id": "l07_8",
   "line": "l07",
   "text": "Prices doubled. Then doubled again.",
   "t0": 34.65,
   "t1": 37.33
  },
  {
   "id": "l07_9",
   "line": "l07",
   "text": "People bought, just to sell a week later, for more.",
   "t0": 37.41,
   "t1": 40.55
  },
  {
   "id": "l08_10",
   "line": "l08",
   "text": "The most famous bulb of all, the Semper Augustus, was said to be worth a mansion.",
   "t0": 41.05,
   "t1": 46.73
  },
  {
   "id": "l09_11",
   "line": "l09",
   "text": "And then, in February 1637, at a sale in Haarlem, the buyers stayed away.",
   "t0": 48.05,
   "t1": 54.49
  },
  {
   "id": "l10_12",
   "line": "l10",
   "text": "Within days, the panic spread. Prices collapsed.",
   "t0": 55.05,
   "t1": 58.63
  },
  {
   "id": "l10_13",
   "line": "l10",
   "text": "People refused to pay for bulbs they had promised to buy.",
   "t0": 59.09,
   "t1": 62.37
  },
  {
   "id": "l11_14",
   "line": "l11",
   "text": "For centuries, it was told as the story of a country ruined.",
   "t0": 63.05,
   "t1": 67.05
  },
  {
   "id": "l11_15",
   "line": "l11",
   "text": "But few people actually went broke.",
   "t0": 67.33,
   "t1": 69.63
  },
  {
   "id": "l11_16",
   "line": "l11",
   "text": "What really broke was trust.",
   "t0": 69.69,
   "t1": 71.63
  },
  {
   "id": "l12_17",
   "line": "l12",
   "text": "And the strangest part?",
   "t0": 72.75,
   "t1": 74.31
  },
  {
   "id": "l12_18",
   "line": "l12",
   "text": "Those flames on the petals were caused by a virus.",
   "t0": 74.35,
   "t1": 77.67
  },
  {
   "id": "l13_19",
   "line": "l13",
   "text": "The most valuable flowers in history were sick.",
   "t0": 78.25,
   "t1": 81.57
  },
  {
   "id": "l13_20",
   "line": "l13",
   "text": "And the sickness was what people paid for.",
   "t0": 81.73,
   "t1": 84.71
  },
  {
   "id": "l14_21",
   "line": "l14",
   "text": "A bubble begins when people stop buying the thing, and start buying the price.",
   "t0": 85.35,
   "t1": 90.57
  }
 ],
